    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including both new acceptance tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation from `city` using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` endpoint responds via `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, and `OwnerDto` is generated from `openapi.yml`. So the change had two parts:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it serializes as `$.locality`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` plus a `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `locality(owner)` default method returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other city \u2014 mirroring the existing derived-field pattern (`membershipTier`, `initials`).\n\nVerified: `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney \u2192 NSW) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random city \u2192 UNKNOWN) both pass, and the full suite builds green.",
